  "details": "1. Look at a user's nameplate who is on mobile platforms or iOS.\n\nCurrently, the platform icons in the new UI are extremely confusing and do not match the icons on world cards, portals, avatar info, or avatar pedestals. This should be uniform on the nameplate as well, but the new UI has a weird tablet icon that at first I was very confused about since it was far too small at default sizes to immediately identify it as such. Realistically, the platform icons should match the existing ones used in all other UI elements in VRChat, such as the world cards, portals, avatar details, and pedestals.[1][2]\n\nAlso, the alignment of the UI element itself is atrocious. I'm not sure why the Username text, the pronouns text, and the platform icon are all at different heights, but that needs to be addressed[3]. I think making sure that they are all bottom-aligned properly would be a good start. Though I would recommend seeing if vertically centering the platform icon would look good. And of course, changing said icons to be the uniformly used icons\n\nI think an elegant solution would be using the platform icons as they currently exist in the other UI, but just without the bordering circle. The colors can match the nameplate instead of being blue, green, and white, as each icon is more than unique enough.",
